chunks.text:
[Pressure]
{the driving low synthesizer eighth-note ostinato on D and very heavy percussion return at once, much more intense than before}
{very low, heavily distorted electric guitars play heavy chugging riffs and power chords in a moving progression D, C, B flat, C}
{doubling the ostinato, a wall of low rumble, no solos and no high guitar}
{the choir sings the chant motif with a fifth above and a low octave below, bells answer}
{the last eight seconds build: drums double their pace, a rising synthesizer riser, the choir swells, everything pushes towards the climax}

[Second Climax]
{the true climax and the biggest moment of the whole piece, clearly louder, denser and bigger than the first climax}
{the full bass choir in open fifths sings the chant motif at full power, with a high choir an octave above, huge reverb}
{very low distorted guitars play thick power chords D, C, B flat, C, huge drums and timpani, cymbal crashes on every bar, a rising synthesizer swell, a massive wall of sound}

[Return]
{everything falls away except the sustained bass choir chord on D, exactly as at the very start of the piece}
{a low drone and one distant bell, no drums, no fade-out, no final hit}
